  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I found the Harborview Supplies email (\"Invoice #4471 - October pallets\"). Our spam filter caught it and held it back. I've asked for it to be released to your inbox, and a technician needs to approve that first. Once they do, the email should appear in your inbox. Please let us know if it hasn't shown up after that. Separately, your account shows as locked after several wrong password attempts on Friday morning. If you have trouble signing in, contact the help desk and we can unlock it for you. Also, there's a file named \"Scanned document 0931.zip\" from docs-share.example in your quarantine. It was flagged as malware, so it will stay blocked. Please don't ask the sender to resend it unless you know who they are.",
  "internal_note": "Followed KB-007. The quarantine for tom.becker (user_id 4) has Q-1004 from billing@harborview-supplies.example, subject \"Invoice #4471 - October pallets\", received 2026-10-11, reason spam, releasable. It matches the user's ticket exactly, and the domain is not a look-alike. Queued release_email for Q-1004 (approval_id 1). I did NOT release Q-1005 (scanner@docs-share.example, \"Scanned document 0931.zip\", malware, not releasable). Other finding: the account status is locked with 5 failed logins. Sign-in logs show the failed_password attempts all came on 2026-10-09 around 09:20-09:35 ET from the corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York, mixed with a successful Duo login. That looks like a cached or mistyped password, not a compromise: no foreign or hosting-network sign-ins and no MFA denials. The user didn't ask for an unlock, so I didn't queue one. I told the user to contact us if he needs it.",
